      "writtenOn": "2023-02-07T15:18:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`copy_slots_unmasked` is using `memcpy` which doesn\u0027t guarantee its behavior when the ranges overlap: https://osscs.corp.google.com/skia/skia/+/main:src/opts/SkRasterPipeline_opts.h;l\u003d3351;drc\u003d5935b0dc422b930b490944c5874c90e33560a633\n\nSo I added in a check to ensure that this overlap can\u0027t occur.\nAnother way to fix this would be to rewrite the copy functions to load everything into registers then store it back out, rather than using memcpy. In practice this is probably going to generate ~the same code. Then we could remove this check. (I actually wrote this version at one point then decided the slot-range check was the safer change.)\n\nI could experiment with this and see how the codegen looks for hand-rolled memcpy. I know this case _does_ actually happen in at least one test, but probably not often enough that it matters. (This block of assignments rolls up: https://osscs.corp.google.com/skia/skia/+/main:tests/sksl/runtime/LargeProgram_Functions.skrp;l\u003d4-8;drc\u003dfb67bdb6c4e94a2a3af6a0b37c85d7d9b35d9ba4 )",
